 		<English>[H1]Sevopedia Votes Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]This page explains abbreviations used in Sevopedia Votes.[PARAGRAPH:2]List abbreviations:[PARAGRAPH:2]- Source prefixes are removed in entries because votes are already grouped by source section headers (for example, United Nations and Apostolic Palace).[PARAGRAPH:2]- E: means Election.[PARAGRAPH:2]- R# means Resolution #.[PARAGRAPH:2]Panel abbreviations:[PARAGRAPH:2]- V.Source means Vote Source.[PARAGRAPH:2]- S.Civic means Vote Source Civic.[PARAGRAPH:2]- S.Free.Sp means Vote Source Free Specialist.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Fo.Civics means Forced Civics.[PARAGRAPH:2]Scope difference:[PARAGRAPH:2]- Vote Source fields (V.Source, S.Civic, S.Free.Sp, Vote Source Info) apply to the vote source itself and are shared by votes that belong to that source.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Vote fields (Requirements, Effects, Fo.Civics) apply to the selected vote/resolution entry.[PARAGRAPH:2]- Full vote names remain visible in the Name panel.</English>
